{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"tmdb","kind":"episodes","input":{"mediaId":22974,"seasonNumber":1},"checkedAt":1793323517633,"status":"ok","value":{"seasonNumber":1,"episodeCount":12,"posters":[],"backgrounds":[],"episodes":[{"id":"617574","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":1,"title":{"value":"Episodio 1","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Two mermaid sisters, Marin and Urin, discover a ring that has fallen in the ocean and attempt to return it to the owner. However, when they find Kanon she refuses to accept the ring and throws it into the forest. Urin gets lost in the forest during a fireworks display and finds a sealed tomb.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2009-06-25","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":24,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/wlzVq8vBigrnVYDe0gfSadimWh0.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/wlzVq8vBigrnVYDe0gfSadimWh0.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/22974/season/1/episode/1"},{"id":"617575","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":2,"title":{"value":"Episodio 2","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"With Sedna's release, darkness washes over the island. Matsumoto, the elder sea turtle, awakens and explains to Marin that she is the Priestess of the Sea. In disbelief, Kanon runs off and is attacked by a creature of darkness.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2009-07-02","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":24,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/ecLC4WZHU47ZC0hLYyv82a3mAQd.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/ecLC4WZHU47ZC0hLYyv82a3mAQd.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/22974/season/1/episode/2"},{"id":"617576","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":3,"title":{"value":"Episodio 3","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Kanon is shocked to discover that Marin, Urin, and Matsumoto have made themselves at home in her house. Marin poses as a fortuneteller to distract Suzuki from finding Kanon, who is hiding, and learns more about Kanon and her mysterious evil aura.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2009-07-09","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":24,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/zPKGpDaQySFfzP9gtAXSeRqtjKj.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/zPKGpDaQySFfzP9gtAXSeRqtjKj.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/22974/season/1/episode/3"},{"id":"617577","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":4,"title":{"value":"Episodio 4","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Matsumoto gives Kanon a treasure map for Kagero Island, hoping that if she finds the treasure it will improve the purity of her heart. After Kanon and Marin leave, Miyako explains to Urin of a legend about a pirate's cursed treasure within the cave.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2009-07-16","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":24,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/xlFvC2d9qY7dajk599KkOQvX9Nh.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/xlFvC2d9qY7dajk599KkOQvX9Nh.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/22974/season/1/episode/4"},{"id":"617578","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":5,"title":{"value":"Episodio 5","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Amamiko Island is abuzz with activity as tourists flock to see the solar eclipse and Matsumoto fears the darkness such an event could invite. Meanwhile, the growing rift between Urin and Marin reaches a breaking point.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2009-07-23","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":24,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/oKHQVOC7OZwdgWd5mYgy75HNE2.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/oKHQVOC7OZwdgWd5mYgy75HNE2.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/22974/season/1/episode/5"},{"id":"617579","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":6,"title":{"value":"Episodio 6","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{